WEBVTT

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.609
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me all right? Teams has picked a different microphone again.</v>

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.089
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, just about.</v>

00:00:16.579 --> 00:00:21.129
<v Aisha Begum>Bit faint, Sarah. Sounds like you're at the other end of the room.</v>

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Hang on... there. Headset rather than the laptop.</v>

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.160
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, that's better.</v>

00:00:27.469 --> 00:00:33.070
<v Callum Reid>While we're getting settled, the broken coffee machine in the canteen has really improved my Wednesday.</v>

00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:38.009
<v Tomasz Nowak>You might have to drink water, Callum. Terrible situation.</v>

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.649
<v Callum Reid>I've got tea. It's not the same relationship.</v>

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.990
<v Jamie Brennan>Brought mine from home. Rookie mistake, relying on that thing.</v>

00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:54.140
<v Fiona Doyle>All right, no need to look quite so pleased with yourself, Jamie.</v>

00:00:55.399 --> 00:01:01.700
<v Sarah Okafor>Between that and the traffic on the ring road, it's a cheerful start. I barely moved for ages.</v>

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.519
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Same. Everyone trying the other lane, then trying to get back in.</v>

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, gaining about half a car length. Anyway, we're here.</v>

00:01:14.599 --> 00:01:16.700
<v Fiona Doyle>Have we got everyone who's coming?</v>

00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:20.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Everyone for today, yeah. Haley's not in.</v>

00:01:21.459 --> 00:01:29.510
<v Sarah Okafor>Haley asked me to pass on where he's got to with chasing the purchase order. He's done the prep; just the write-up left.</v>

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.189
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, cheers for passing that on.</v>

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:36.359
<v Sarah Okafor>Tommo, yours?</v>

00:01:36.739 --> 00:01:41.290
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, the near-miss write-up for the pop valve is finished. All signed off.</v>

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:44.489
<v Callum Reid>Good stuff.</v>

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:52.700
<v Sarah Okafor>And my contractor booking for the desiccant unit is sorted. They've actually been in as well—no issues found.</v>

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:55.140
<v Aisha Begum>Oh, that's reassuring.</v>

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, nice to have a straightforward one.</v>

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:03.870
<v Fiona Doyle>Sarah, what about the timing for sending the shift handover report round?</v>

00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:10.400
<v Sarah Okafor>That's moved. I'll send the shift handover report round by the end of the week now.</v>

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:13.900
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, thanks.</v>

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.979
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, today's new bits. Not a massive list.</v>

00:02:20.199 --> 00:02:21.400
<v Aisha Begum>Go on.</v>

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:30.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Tommo, can you grease and check the bearings on the Main Outfeed Conveyor by the 28th? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:34.830
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, I can't take that on, sorry. I haven't got the capacity.</v>

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Olumide Adeyemi, can you take that instead?</v>

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.900
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The bearings on the Main Outfeed Conveyor, grease and check, yeah?</v>

00:02:46.969 --> 00:02:52.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, that's it. By the 28th, and as I say, it matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:57.810
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll take it. I'll grease and check the bearings.</v>

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.909
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, got that.</v>

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:05.599
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, took me a second. Someone started speaking next to me.</v>

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.789
<v Tomasz Nowak>Thought you were pretending the connection had gone.</v>

00:03:10.939 --> 00:03:14.439
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, no. My frozen face is usually much more convincing.</v>

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:18.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Callum, you were coming in there?</v>

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:25.219
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, so, the near miss at the new line needs writing up. I'll write that up.</v>

00:03:26.389 --> 00:03:28.840
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, that's worth having properly written down.</v>

00:03:29.939 --> 00:03:31.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Callum. That's yours, then.</v>

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.080
<v Callum Reid>Yep, I'll do the write-up.</v>

00:03:36.479 --> 00:03:41.379
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, did I talk over someone then? I got a sort of double voice.</v>

00:03:42.939 --> 00:03:45.039
<v Aisha Begum>You're all right. We heard Callum.</v>

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:52.539
<v Jamie Brennan>Ah, okay. It's doing that thing where everyone goes quiet, then all the sound arrives at once.</v>

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:58.270
<v Fiona Doyle>Yes. Usually makes it sound like we're having a much bigger argument than we are.</v>

00:04:00.219 --> 00:04:03.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything else we actually need to agree this morning?</v>

00:04:05.009 --> 00:04:06.409
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nothing else from me.</v>

00:04:07.949 --> 00:04:09.349
<v Aisha Begum>No, I'm all right.</v>

00:04:11.319 --> 00:04:12.520
<v Jamie Brennan>Nothing from stores.</v>

00:04:14.289 --> 00:04:15.490
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No more here.</v>

00:04:16.879 --> 00:04:18.079
<v Fiona Doyle>I'm good, thanks.</v>

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we'll leave it there. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:25.329
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. Back to my disappointing tea.</v>

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:28.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Enjoy that. Bye, all.</v>
